From: OpenWrt
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: realtek_otto: do not sleep in the restart handler

otto_wdt_restart() masks the phase 1 interrupt with disable_irq(), which
waits for running handlers through synchronize_irq() and, on current
kernels, for an RCU grace period. The restart handler runs after
machine_restart() has stopped the other CPUs. If the RCU grace period
kthread last ran on a stopped CPU, the grace period never completes,
disable_irq() never returns and the reset register is never written.
The system then hangs at "reboot: Restarting system" with RCU stall
reports instead of resetting.

On a dual core RTL9303 this hung 3 of 22 and 1 of 18 warm reboots, with
the reboot task blocked in otto_wdt_restart -> __synchronize_irq ->
synchronize_rcu_normal.

Use disable_irq_nosync(). Only masking the interrupt is needed: the
handler cannot usefully run once the reset has been requested.
---
--- a/drivers/watchdog/realtek_otto_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/realtek_otto_wdt.c
@@ -167,7 +167,7 @@
 	u32 reset_mode;
 	u32 v;
 
-	disable_irq(ctrl->irq_phase1);
+	disable_irq_nosync(ctrl->irq_phase1);
 
 	switch (reboot_mode) {
 	case REBOOT_SOFT:
